                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a415a7c2-b201-4c13-a7a4-bb743bd8aaf1",
                                "sense_id": "f162f1fb-c290-360e-9f01-a7785d0a3074",
                                "text": "The First parte of the Mirour on its first appearance, in 1574, included sixteen tragedies and ended with the tragedy of Nennius, after which a conclusion was made in a lenvoy of five stanzas."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20caf98a-5388-41d8-b166-ba3542109da3",
                                "sense_id": "f162f1fb-c290-360e-9f01-a7785d0a3074",
                                "text": "Ladies! Lenvoy to you that have this prize; I reed ye hold your owne, if you be wise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3f54acc-79cf-4ea8-b656-591c6b680483",
                                "sense_id": "f162f1fb-c290-360e-9f01-a7785d0a3074",
                                "text": "For at the end of Bk. II. there is a lenvoy, commencing \"Rome, remember of thy foundation\"; it is one of the best of Lydgate's remarkable lenvoys, rendered pompous and sonorous by the monotony of its rhyme-system, for it has only three rhymes in its 126 lines (133 in Tottel's)!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
